<div style="background-color: #1a5276; color: white; padding: 15px; text-align: center; border-radius: 8px;">
    <h1 style="margin: 0;">Lesson Planner – Theme # ___ – Lesson # 3</h1>
    <p style="margin: 5px 0 0 0;"><em>Complete this planner five times per theme, once per lesson (Lesson 1 through Lesson 5).</em></p>
</div>

<table style="border: 1px dashed #333; border-collapse: collapse; width: 100%; margin: 10px 0;">
    <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px; width: 50%;"><b>Lesson #:</b> 3</td>
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px; width: 50%;"><b>Skills Focus:</b> Speaking</td>
    </tr>
    <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><b>Grade:</b> 5th Grade (CEFR: A1.3)</td>
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><b>Scenario:</b> Taking Care of Our Class</td>
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><b>Theme:</b> We Are Sweeping the Floors.</td>
    </tr>
    <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><b>Date(s):</b> From ___ to ___</td>
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;" colspan="2"><b>Learning Sequence Time:</b> 45–50 min</td>
    </tr>
    <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;" colspan="3">
            <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Specific Objective:</b> Speaking: Productive: Give simple directions within the school. Interactive: Participate in short conversations about familiar topics.</p>
            <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Learning Outcome:</b> Speaking: Can give simple directions to find places in the school (e.g., "The cleaning area is next to the bathroom."). Can participate in short conversations about familiar tasks (e.g., "What are you doing?" "I am arranging the desks."). Can ask and answer questions about their favorite activities (e.g., "Can you help me clean the classroom, please?" "Yes, I can clean up the board.").</p>
        </td>
    </tr>
</table>

<h2 style="color: #1a5276;">The Six Action-Oriented Approach (AOA) Lesson Stages</h2>
<table style="border: 1px dashed #333; border-collapse: collapse; width: 100%; margin: 10px 0;">
    <thead>
        <tr style="background-color: #f0f0f0;">
            <th style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px; width: 30%; color: #1a5276;">Stage & Description</th>
            <th style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px; width: 50%; color: #1a5276;">Activities & Teacher Actions</th>
            <th style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px; width: 20%; color: #1a5276;">Estimated Date and Time</th>
        </tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
        <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <h3 style="color: #1a5276; margin-top: 0;">STAGE 1 — Warm-up / Pre-task</h3>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">Engagement, Modeling and Clarification.</p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Warm-up: "What's Missing?"</b></p>
                <ul style="list-style-type: disc; padding-left: 20px;">
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">The teacher places various classroom items and cleaning supplies (e.g., chair, desk, whiteboard, door, trash can, mop, bucket, cloth) on a table or displays pictures on the board.</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Students close their eyes. The teacher removes one item.</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Students open their eyes and say, "The [item] is missing!" in pairs or individually.</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Teacher encourages students to ask, "What is missing?" and answer, "The [mop] is missing."</li>
                </ul>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Modeling:</b></p>
                <ul style="list-style-type: disc; padding-left: 20px;">
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">The teacher models key phrases for giving simple directions and offering help: "Let's sweep the floor.", "Can you help me wipe the desks?", "Please arrange the chairs."</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">The teacher explicitly models pronunciation of /r/ in "arrange" and /s/ in "supply," asking students to repeat.</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">The teacher demonstrates the action for each verb (sweep, wipe, arrange, organize) while saying the word, linking action to meaning.</li>
                </ul>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Clarification (CCQs):</b></p>
                <ul style="list-style-type: disc; padding-left: 20px;">
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Teacher shows a picture of someone sweeping: "Is he reading a book?" (No.) "What is he doing?" (He is sweeping.)</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Teacher shows a mop and asks: "Is this for wiping windows?" (No.) "What is it for?" (It's for sweeping floors.)</li>
                </ul>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">5-7 min</td>
        </tr>
        <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <h3 style="color: #1a5276; margin-top: 0;">STAGE 2 — Presentation</h3>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">Input of new language/content connected to Scenario: "Taking Care of Our Class".</p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Material:</b> Illustrated dialogue or picture sequence with captions depicting students cleaning their classroom.</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Communicative Competence:</b> Understanding and responding to simple instructions and questions about familiar tasks and places in the school.</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Detailed Procedure:</b></p>
                <ul style="list-style-type: disc; padding-left: 20px;">
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">The teacher presents a simple illustrated dialogue about two friends, Maria and Carlos, cleaning their classroom.</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Example dialogue:
                        <ul>
                            <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Maria: "Carlos, what are you doing?"</li>
                            <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Carlos: "I am arranging the desks. They are messy."</li>
                            <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Maria: "Oh, I see. Can I help you sweep the floor?"</li>
                            <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Carlos: "Yes, please! The broom and dustpan are next to the door."</li>
                            <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Maria: "Okay! I am sweeping quickly."</li>
                            <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Carlos: "Great! Let's clean the whiteboard, too."</li>
                        </ul>
                    </li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">The teacher reads the dialogue aloud clearly, pointing to the pictures, and using gestures. Students listen.</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">The teacher reads again, and students repeat chorally and individually, focusing on intonation and specific words like "arrange" and "supply".</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>Comprehension tasks:</b>
                        <ul>
                            <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>Gist question:</b> "What are Maria and Carlos doing?" (Cleaning the classroom.)</li>
                            <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>True/False:</b> "Maria is sweeping the whiteboard. True or False?" (False.) "Carlos is arranging the chairs. True or False?" (True.)</li>
                            <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>Information matching:</b> Match pictures of cleaning tasks (e.g., sweeping, wiping, arranging) with sentences from the dialogue.</li>
                        </ul>
                    </li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Teacher highlights compound words like "whiteboard" and practices syllable division: "white-board."</li>
                </ul>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">10-12 min</td>
        </tr>
        <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <h3 style="color: #1a5276; margin-top: 0;">STAGE 3 — Preparation / Practice</h3>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">Accuracy focus on Speaking.</p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Communicative Skill & Content:</b> Using Present Continuous for ongoing actions, Imperatives for instructions, and Modal "can" for offering/asking for help. Vocabulary: chair, desk, mop, bucket, sweep, wipe, arrange, tidy, clean up, please.</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Detailed Procedure:</b></p>
                <ul style="list-style-type: disc; padding-left: 20px;">
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>Activity 1: "Describe the Picture!" (Controlled Practice)</b>
                        <ul>
                            <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">The teacher displays pictures of individuals doing various cleaning tasks (e.g., a girl sweeping, a boy wiping a desk, another student arranging chairs).</li>
                            <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Students, first chorally then individually, describe the actions using the present continuous: "She is sweeping the floor.", "He is wiping the desk.", "They are arranging the chairs."</li>
                            <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Teacher provides sentence frames on the board: "He/She is ______ the ______." or "They are ______ the ______."</li>
                        </ul>
                    </li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>Activity 2: "Give an Instruction!" (Semi-controlled Substitution)</b>
                        <ul>
                            <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Teacher shows flashcards with cleaning verbs (sweep, wipe, arrange, tidy) and objects (floor, whiteboard, desks, chairs).</li>
                            <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">In pairs, one student picks a verb and an object flashcard, and gives an imperative instruction to their partner, using "please": "Sweep the floor, please." or "Please wipe the whiteboard."</li>
                            <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">The partner responds by miming the action and saying, "Okay, I am sweeping the floor." or "Yes, I can wipe the whiteboard."</li>
                        </ul>
                    </li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>Activity 3: "Can You Help Me?" (Pair Interaction)</b>
                        <ul>
                            <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Students work in pairs. Each pair receives a set of picture cards showing different parts of the classroom needing cleaning or organizing.</li>
                            <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Student A points to a card and asks, "Can you help me clean the [desk]?" or "Can you help me [sweep] the floor?"</li>
                            <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Student B responds using "Yes, I can..." or "No, I can't...". If "Yes," they can add what they *are* doing or *will* do. "Yes, I can wipe the desks." or "Yes, I can sweep the floor quickly."</li>
                            <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">They switch roles. Teacher circulates, monitoring for correct use of 'can' and politeness markers.</li>
                        </ul>
                    </li>
                </ul>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">15-17 min</td>
        </tr>
        <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <h3 style="color: #1a5276; margin-top: 0;">STAGE 4 — Performance / Production</h3>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">Communicative task where students USE the language in a realistic scenario: "Taking Care of Our Class".</p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Task Format: "Classroom Cleaning Crew" Role-Play</b></p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Connection to Theme/Scenario:</b> Students simulate cleaning their own classroom, assigning tasks, and offering help, using all practiced language.</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Focus:</b> Fluency, collaborative interaction, giving and following simple directions, offering help politely, and using target vocabulary and grammar.</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Detailed Procedure:</b></p>
                <ul style="list-style-type: disc; padding-left: 20px;">
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Students work in groups of 3-4. Each group is assigned a "zone" or part of the classroom (e.g., "front of the classroom," "back of the classroom," "windows and door area").</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Each group discusses and plans what needs to be cleaned or organized in their zone using the target vocabulary (e.g., "The desks are messy.", "We need to sweep the floor.").</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">One student acts as the "leader" and assigns tasks or asks for help using imperatives and 'can': "Please wipe the whiteboard, [Name]." "Can you help me arrange these chairs?"</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Other group members respond by accepting the task, offering help, or asking for clarification: "Yes, I can wipe it carefully." "I am sweeping the floor quickly." "Let's put away the books."</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Students use realia (if available and safe, or pretend) like cloths, sponges, or mops to enhance the role-play.</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">The teacher circulates, listens to conversations, and provides light support, focusing on fluent communication rather than perfect accuracy.</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Each group briefly presents their "clean classroom" and explains what they did (e.g., "We are sweeping the floor.", "He is arranging the desks.").</li>
                </ul>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">10-12 min</td>
        </tr>
        <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <h3 style="color: #1a5276; margin-top: 0;">STAGE 5 — Assessment / Post-task</h3>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">Formative assessment strategy.</p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Formative Assessment Strategy: Teacher Observation Checklist for Speaking</b></p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Assessment Task:</b> Students participate in the "Classroom Cleaning Crew" role-play.</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Evaluation Criteria (Teacher Checklist):</b></p>
                <ul style="list-style-type: disc; padding-left: 20px;">
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>Use of Present Continuous:</b> Can use "I am sweeping" or "He is cleaning."</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>Use of Imperatives:</b> Can give simple instructions like "Sweep the floor, please."</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>Use of Modal "Can":</b> Can ask for/offer help (e.g., "Can you help me?", "Yes, I can.").</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>Vocabulary Use:</b> Incorporates at least 5 target cleaning/classroom words.</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>Politeness:</b> Uses "please" when giving instructions or making requests.</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>Intelligibility:</b> Pronunciation is clear enough for partners to understand.</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>Collaboration:</b> Actively participates and interacts with group members.</li>
                </ul>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Student Self-Assessment / Exit Ticket:</b> Students complete these sentences:</p>
                <ul style="list-style-type: disc; padding-left: 20px;">
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Today, I can say "I am ____________" to describe what I am doing.</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">One new thing I learned to say in English is: "Can you help me ____________?"</li>
                </ul>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">5-7 min</td>
        </tr>
        <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <h3 style="color: #1a5276; margin-top: 0;">STAGE 6 — Reflection</h3>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">Student and Teacher reflection.</p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Student Self-Reflection:</b></p>
                <ul style="list-style-type: disc; padding-left: 20px;">
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">What was your favorite cleaning task to talk about today?</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">What was easy or difficult about giving instructions or offering help in English?</li>
                </ul>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Teacher Reflection:</b></p>
                <ul style="list-style-type: disc; padding-left: 20px;">
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">What worked well in this speaking lesson? (e.g., student engagement in role-play, use of specific grammar points).</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">What adjustments or scaffolds are needed for students who struggled with speaking (e.g., more sentence frames, less complex tasks, more explicit pronunciation practice)?</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">How can the use of "please" and "let's" be further reinforced in future lessons to foster collaboration and politeness?</li>
                </ul>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Connection to next lesson:</b> This lesson focused on speaking about cleaning tasks. The next lesson (Lesson 4: Writing) will build on this by having students write short descriptions or instructions about cleaning their classroom or school areas, solidifying their understanding and usage of the vocabulary and grammar in written form.</p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">3-5 min</td>
        </tr>
    </tbody>
</table>